    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49751" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unctŭlus</span></b> , a, um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj. dim.</i>
			[unctus, from ungo], <i>besmeared</i>, <i>anointed.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: circumtonsi et terti atque unctuli, Varr.
			ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 179, 8</span></i>.—*
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unctŭlum</span></b> , i, n.,
				<i>a little ointment</i>,
				<i><span class="en">App. M. 3, p. 139, 2</span></i>.</div>
